# Naming

- Use descriptive names. Spell words out instead of abbreviating them.
- Extract a compound condition into a descriptive local before passing it as a keyword argument when the name explains what the condition means.
- Omit the leading underscore on classes introduced as named result models.
- Name a function for its action: a verb phrase that says what it does and returns (`parse_server_entries`, not `server_entries`). A noun-only name hides the intent.
- A function does one thing. If its name needs "and", split it.

Why: code is read far more often than it is written.

